    {"id": 1, "claim": "Modern archaeological and historical consensus rejects the 'single origin' theory of Chinese civilization in favor of a 'multi-origin' or 'plurality' model.", "evidence": "Scholars like Li Feng and archaeological findings (e.g., Liangzhu, Longshan, Shijiahe cultures) demonstrate that complex societies emerged independently in various regions (Yellow River, Yangtze River, West, etc.) before unification.", "weight": 0.9, "depends_on": []},
